  "handRegistered": {
    "reason": "HomeDrawer is not a `*Page` struct, so `extract_ios_pages.py` does not generate a contract for it. PR22 made it the product drawer (`NativeShell.swift:238` `SessionsDrawerPanel` → `HomeDrawer`), which is a real surface with its own session/folder/settings controls, so it must not disappear from the gate.",
    "mechanism": "a whole contract file, not a `_spec-required.json` entry: that file merges items into an extracted contract, and the extractor has no `*Page` contract to merge into. `extract_ios_pages.py` never writes or deletes `pages/home-drawer.json`; `check_chrome_contracts` verifies this file and its declared struct still exist, and `page_structure_check.py` compares it like every other contract, provenance included.",
    "homeSpec": "`HomeSpec.swift` is the 430x932 value authority behind this drawer and ChatPage (page #F7F7F7, text #1A1A1A, 16/24 body, 16 chrome vs 20 content inset, radii and spacing). It declares no View struct, so it has no page contract of its own; `extract_ios_pages.py` pins the file in CHROME_VALUE_FILES and README §1.1 records it."
  },
